{"resourceIdentifier":"3072","resourceName":"Rwanda Riparian Restoration Project","description":"The Rwanda Riparian Restoration Project is restoring riparian buffer zones in key watersheds and catchment areas within the mountainous areas of Rwanda. These buffer zones serve a critical ecological function as the interface between sensitive upland areas and the water resources that they buffer. The project is using select species of sympodial (clumping) bamboos. These planted bamboo clumps have an intricate underground root system that binds fragile soils and reduces erosion and loss of top soil from sloping agricultural lands. In addition this root system reduces siltation, protecting water resources for downstream users. The multi-dimensional bamboo canopy further serves to reduce the rate and volume of flow of rainfall into rivers reducing flooding, and protecting river banks. \r\n\r\nThe planted bamboo is purely for conservation and environmental purposes, while having high carbon emission removal benefits as a permanent and carbon rich ecosystem.","location":{"latitude":-2.124233,"longitude":29.615147},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2025-06-11","endExclusive":"2025-07-12","endInclusive":"2025-07-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3072"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Karongi"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"EcoPlanet Bamboo Group, LLC"},{"type":"string","value":"DE, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"+254-721-999-604"},{"type":"string","value":"crebelo@ecoplanetbamboo.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Verification approval requested"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"51964"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry an